# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values there. .env is gitignored
# and never committed — only the variable *names* belong in version
# control, never the values (same principle as kbguard.yaml's
# api_key_env: fields, which hold a variable name, not a secret).
#
# .env is loaded automatically by the repo-root conftest.py before any
# test runs (python-dotenv) — nothing else in kbguard reads it.

# Remote Docker host for pgvector/Qdrant contract tests, if not localhost.
# See docs/project/contributing.md.
# KBGUARD_TEST_PG_HOST=
# KBGUARD_TEST_PG_PORT=5434
# KBGUARD_TEST_QDRANT_HOST=
# KBGUARD_TEST_QDRANT_PORT=6333

# Pinecone: needed only for tests/test_adapters_pinecone_live.py, which is
# skipped automatically when these aren't set. Free "Starter" tier is
# enough — see docs/guide/adapters/pinecone.md.
# PINECONE_API_KEY=
# PINECONE_TEST_INDEX=

# judge.model in kbguard.yaml is a plain litellm model string -- only the
# ONE matching provider's key below is actually needed, based on whatever
# you set judge.model to (e.g. judge.model: xai/grok-4.5 needs only
# XAI_API_KEY; judge.model: ollama/llama3 needs none of these at all,
# since Ollama runs locally with no API key). Fill in only the one(s)
# you're actually going to use.
# xAI / Grok -- judge.model: xai/grok-4.5 (or whatever's current on x.ai's pricing page)
# XAI_API_KEY=
# Groq (fast/cheap inference for open models -- NOT the same company as
# Grok/xAI, confusingly similar name) -- judge.model: groq/qwen/qwen3.8-27b
# recommended over groq/openai/gpt-oss-120b: hand-verified both are real,
# callable model names, but at temperature=0 gpt-oss-120b consistently
# misjudges a real planted contradiction that qwen3.8-27b consistently
# gets right (see tests/conftest.py's real_judge fixture)
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# OpenAI -- judge.model: gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Anthropic -- judge.model: anthropic/claude-3-5-sonnet-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
